#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:5
#: 3843cef1b4cf499bb5af06067ab2d43d
msgid "Archived: Migration from Plane 3.7 to 3.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:7
#: 67e4037bbe59461bbc9a5416c0fe7450
msgid "This is a guide to migrating from plane 3.7 to plane 3.8. There have been a large number of configuration changes, so please read the guide carefully, and make sure you do careful ground tests before your first flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:12
#: 11dbd54100184113be59a28c0aa0c5d6
msgid "The firmware will try to auto-migrate your parameters where possible, but it is a complex migration and there is the possibility of errors, so careful testing is critical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:18
#: 7af9e116dec640ae900405ee9cdf0402
msgid "If you later downgrade from Plane 3.8 to an earlier version, then any changes that were made to the RC_* and SERVOn_* parameters will be lost. Upgrading back to 3.8 (or higher) will not copy over any new param changes. This is only an issue if the user decides to downgrade. **Please note that downgrading from 3.8 to 3.7 (or earlier) is very likely to cause a crash if you do not manually restore channel reversals.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:26
#: 6b86e5a1710f4082819b1db9e87058ed
msgid "Change to Servo Range Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:28
#: 56345a71c70f4693aacd420fd1debe96
msgid "One of the biggest changes between plane 3.7 and 3.8 is the change from RCn_* parameters to SERVOn_* parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:31
#: 48a462b04f3944fd8ac3a49a306a885a
msgid "In plane 3.7 and before, the range, trim and function of all input and output channels was controlled by a single set of parameters starting with RC. For example, the handling of input channel 1 was defined by 4 parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:36
#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:48
#: 49c8a7bf7d0a4167ab14ece17d097e25
#: bbce533bdf69403ea52284391da5be44
msgid "RC1_MIN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:37
#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:49
#: f4e2280d7d0d4e8fa2533179e4fec55c
#: 36b72e017d7b4db393428a9d71efb20e
msgid "RC1_MAX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:38
#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:50
#: 8af56f1e4eaa415fb5d2c31d81b39997
#: db54d3bba73044b6945c8d2668406996
msgid "RC1_TRIM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:39
#: e225b561217045a990e1a18c54af101f
msgid "RC1_REV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:42
#: a4662210d49f42ada1b6803334ccb958
msgid "these same parameters also controlled the range of output values for the first output channel. That means you could not have a different range for your RC inputs and your servo outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:46
#: 0a226a4d26204de0b87cf8ccc2205256
msgid "In plane 3.8 the above 4 parameters are replaced with 8 parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:51
#: f1976d862f07454faa5ffe3fe4294184
msgid "RC1_REVERSED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:52
#: 98dfea072b3d48b0a3351e5c99ffb4a4
msgid "SERVO1_MIN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:53
#: 64c458462c1f45239dae67012d35448d
msgid "SERVO1_MAX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:54
#: 0203d0fc35124189a5bd6089149b3df0
msgid "SERVO1_TRIM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:55
#: 56d613eeb74140da8b6b7fef8442ffe5
msgid "SERVO1_REVERSED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:57
#: ecced813bbdb4251b239ab2e51a4b17c
msgid "the RC parameters control an input channel, the SERVO parameters control an output channel. This gives much more flexibility, and means that when you re-calibrate your RC inputs it doesn't affect the tuning of your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:62
#: 8873ed2492554a928a950bc2ffca5502
msgid "You may also notice that the \"REV\" parameters have been renamed to \"REVERSED\". This is because the old parameters had a convention so that \"reversed\" was chosen by setting RC1_REV to -1, and \"not reversed\" was chosen by setting RC1_REV to 1. This caused quite a lot of confusion, so for 3.8 we now use the convention that RC1_REVERSED=0 means not reversed and RC1_REVERSED=1 means reversed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:70
#: bb35f1a29814469aa8ce32f5c6dc4c8e
msgid "Change to Servo Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:72
#: fe43522c6cdd434283f73a3bf613d798
msgid "The second big change is to the parameters that defines what each output is used for. In plane 3.7 the output function of the first 4 channels was hard coded, following the AETR \"aileron, elevator, throttle, rudder\" convention. Channels 5 and above had FUNCTION parameters, allowing their function to be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:78
#: 8a327b8f2dff42dd8431ce61207479bc
msgid "For example, in plane 3.7 you could set RC5_FUNCTION to 4 to make output channel 5 an additional aileron."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:81
#: ad57b35cfa26406aa302d3433cc93faf
msgid "In plane 3.8 the functions are chosen using the SERVOn_FUNCTION parameters. You can set these on any output channel. The default for the first 4 channels is the same, but you can change it to any output type you like. This gives a lot more flexibility, and is especially useful for flight boards with a smaller number of output channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:87
#: 562339fdb7d441189d6e22a5adf98047
msgid "So if you wanted the 5th output channel to be an aileron you could set SERVO5_FUNCTION=4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:90
#: 28740fb6c2fa49e1821b7e1573b898d3
msgid "You can see more details on output functions in the :ref:`Output Functions <channel-output-functions>` documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:93
#: 89d2643d345f4917aa3e4048cee24e0c
msgid "Change to Elevon, Vtail and Flaperon Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:95
#: 8c98b7c165124fee93464ececab24a5f
msgid "The method of setting up elevon, vtail and flaperon planes has completely changed in plane 3.8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:98
#: c58a5c5430f64c0b992ed411acb9b902
msgid "In the 3.7 release if you wanted to setup an elevon plane you would set the variable ELEVON_OUTPUT to an integer from 1 to 8. This then changed the behaviour of the first aileron and elevator channel to do elevon mixing. The value of ELEVON_OUTPUT controlled the possible channel order and reversal options (8 combinations are possible)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:104
#: f2f6c76614a2458ca67b8ec0746340eb
msgid "In plane 3.8 a much simpler and more flexible system is used. If you want channel 1 to be a left elevon and channel 2 to be a right elevon then you use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:108
#: 569b46d91d8d44e69c76c790cf28f6a7
msgid "SERVO1_FUNCTION=77"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:109
#: abc8a6b8e6e947f0ade9e93106d48d97
msgid "SERVO2_FUNCTION=78"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:111
#: 42e0a7bb96b14a9e97efdc95725de25d
msgid "the value 77 means \"left elevon\". The value 78 means \"right elevon\". You can then set the reversals as needed, using SERVO1_REVERSED and SERVO2_REVERSED."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:115
#: 3c6f3730caf1440083d8af35bbac98a2
msgid "Changing to this system means you can have elevons on any channel (and multiple elevons if needed), plus you can directly control the trim and range of each elevon,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:119
#: 859202a9675d45e184abaacc25f66017
msgid "The same system is used for vtail, flaperon and differential spoiler setups. Please see the following guides for more details:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:122
#: 58fc21f42070438aae6d66fc15ec71f7
msgid ":ref:`Elevon Planes <guide-elevon-plane>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:123
#: 143b004e6c6942bbab699ef10fc4beef
msgid ":ref:`VTail Planes <guide-vtail-plane>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:124
#: bf66fc6c117a48c2b2dbc2c3da78b82b
msgid ":ref:`Differential Spoilers <differential-spoilers>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:125
#: 1827334b932645cbb6ece5f857047d9d
msgid ":ref:`Flaperons <flaperons-on-plane>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:129
#: 87d00508ef2d41feb63d65a134292132
msgid "Tuning Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:131
#: 20bd0db383da47bcbe12216de82dde03
msgid "Some users may notice the tuning of their aircraft changes a bit between 3.7 and 3.8. The likely cause of this is the change in the RC and SERVO parameters. With the separation of the RCn_MIN/MAX parameters from the SERVOn_MIN/MAX parameters you may find that the \"throw\" of your servos changes a bit, which can affect tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:137
#: 29307859ac314da780809597af3291ba
msgid "While the automatic upgrade when you install plane 3.8 onto a plane running 3.7 should produce a very similar servo range, please do check it carefully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:142
#: 8ded61ce573e447ba35d242a59c7d5e3
msgid "Reversal Checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:144
#: 2b89574e78db431db1d0f493b35af96e
msgid "Please do very careful checking for servo reversal before your first flight with plane 3.8. The automatic parameter upgrade when you install plane 3.8 should get this right, but it is very complex and there may be some situations that aren't covered. Please make sure that both of the following are checked carefully after you update:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:150
#: 95b2aad4efac401fbd6d09a492a0fa4d
msgid "that RC inputs give the correct movements of your control surfaces in MANUAL mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:152
#: 49b989279290492d98e39cacbb7c13a3
msgid "that the control surfaces move in the right direction in FBWA mode when you roll and pitch the aircraft with no RC input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:155
#: 0b97803fb1a34061916945e7fd2af74a
msgid "There is a detailed guide to checking for reversals in the :ref:`four channel plane <guide-four-channel-plane>` document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:158
#: e8213d06f51443199e34a82cc8790289
msgid "Airspeed Setup Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:160
#: c6eefc625c334661a7df4c95a6473547
msgid "The parameter for enabling an airspeed sensor has changed from ARSPD_ENABLE in plane 3.7 to ARSPD_TYPE in plane 3.8. This change was made to provide a more flexible way of supporting multiple airspeed sensor types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:165
#: cc4f54a335124f19b321ea3ffd604b32
msgid "If you have a MS4525 digital airspeed sensor then the parameter upgrade should happen automatically and you should find that ARSPD_TYPE will be automatically set to 1. However if you have an analog airspeed sensor then you will need to set ARSPD_TYPE=2 after updating to plane 3.8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:171
#: b9bf0049d5444e46b9616347496c42fd
msgid "Plane 3.8 also supports the new MS5525 airspeed sensor. That is selected by setting ARSPD_TYPE=3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:175
#: e45733b97bea4b98905f2d1af8a4c48a
msgid "Change to THR_MAX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/plane-3-7-to-3-8-migration.rst:177
#: f7bd30aebe934cb3b6a384ad27677dd4
msgid "The THR_MAX parameter, which controls maximum throttle, defaulted to 75 percent for versions 3.7.1 and earlier. In plane 3.8.0 it defaults to 100 percent. If you had not previously changed this parameter and your plane is overpowered at 100 percent throttle you may wish to change it back to 75."
msgstr ""
